 new.\n38-- `TestEmbeddedArchitectureLoadsAsLLMScanner`, `TestArchitectureInHostUntrusted`, `TestArchitecturePromptContract`, `TestArchitecturePromptExamplesDecode` (`internal/roles/architecture_test.go`) as in step 7.\n39-- initcmd tests: `starterTree` match and the PR body mentions the architecture scanner (`internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go`).\n40-- Failure cases: an example whose path is missing from `files`, uses an uppercase rule or has a space in the fingerprint must fail `CheckLLMFingerprints`; the test proves the examples would be caught if they drift.\n41-- Edge: a repo with no ADRs; the prompt instructs an empty output file (checked by the contract test through a sentence match).\n42-\n43-### Risk\n44-Low to medium. No Go logic changes; the change adds an embedded prompt and config. The prompt ships to every `ard init` adopter and runs unattended on a timer in host mode (#84) at up to $2 per run, so a maintainer should read it before merge. `internal/roles/` is not in `merge.protected_paths`, so nothing forces that review. No migrations or concurrency. Rolling the scanner into this repository's own `.ard/scanners/` and `.ard/config.yaml` (protected paths) is left to a human after a `--dry-run` smoke run.\n45-\n46-### Size\n47-S to M (about 250 changed lines, mostly the prompt and tests). Files: `internal/roles/scanners/architecture/prompt.txt` (new), `internal/roles/architecture_test.go` (new), `internal/roles/config.yaml`, `internal/roles/roles.go`, `internal/roles/roles_test.go`, `internal/initcmd/body.go`, `internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go`, `docs/proposal.md`, `docs/layout.md`, `docs/site/roles/scanners.md`.\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nAdds the starter LLM scanner `scanners/architecture`: a prompt that checks code against ADRs and architecture docs and writes findings with stable `<rule>:<path>[:<symbol>]` fingerprints, plus its config override and `ard init` wiring.\n\n## Changes\n- `internal/roles/scanners/architecture/prompt